\section*{Detailed Local Development/Testnet Architecture}

\textbf{Current stack: ink! 6 + pallet-revive}

\textbf{Parachain A (Rights Management Chain)} is the \textbf{content-rights-parachain} runtime with \textbf{pallet-revive} (ink! 6 / PolkaVM) and ink! 6 contracts. When using the single-parachain Zombienet config (\texttt{my-content-rights.toml}), the parachain RPC is \textbf{ws://127.0.0.1:9990}.

\bigskip\hrule\bigskip

This is a detailed local development/testnet architecture for a cross-chain content rights management service. It exemplifies a practical configuration that can be executed on a single high-performance development machine. The objective is to replicate as comprehensively as possible the genuine Polkadot ecosystem locally, encompassing the relay chain, numerous parachains, RMRK collections, ink! contracts, and a fundamental bridge simulation.

